hypertext
{
<tab><cl=F0F010>MAP<cl=A2A2A2><br><br>
<tab>If your character has a map of the area, then by calling it on the screen, you can increase/ decrease the transparency of the map (by clicking on the buttons with the image "+" or "-", respectively), and also see the location of your character (an icon with the image of a little man). If your character has an inkwell, you can independently put various objects on the map (monsters, houses, castles, cities, bridges, caves, ruins, etc.). To do this, click on the button with the image of the "mainland" (located next to "-"). In the window that opens, pictograms with the names of objects are located at the bottom. Click on them with the left mouse button (in this case, the object will be "glued" to the cursor), then click on the required place on the map and the object will be plotted. If necessary, you can sign the object plotted on the map. Click on it (it will start flashing), enter the signature in the edit window, then click on an arbitrary place on the map so that the signature appears on the map.<br>
<tab>You can also put a mark on the map that is displayed on the compass as a risk (for example, the mission objective is displayed). To do this, left-click on a large map while holding down the Shift key. To delete such a label, you need to click on the label removal button (the rightmost button at the bottom of the map) while holding down the Shift key.
}